<title>FRANCE: French consumer spending fell 0.8 pct in Nov.</title>
<headline>French consumer spending fell 0.8 pct in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted figures for household spending on manufactured goods in billions of 1980 francs:</p>
<p>					    Nov    Oct     Sep	Nov 95</p>
<p> Total				   57.61  58.09   59.87     57.49</p>
<p> Total change (pct v pvs month)   -0.8   -3.0    -1.2	 4.4</p>
<p> Retail sector			 39.10  38.09   37.16     38.36</p>
<p> Durables				16.73  17.66   20.35     16.86</p>
<p> Textiles, leather		   11.39  11.11   10.35     11.42</p>
<p> Other				   29.49  29.32   29.16     29.20</p>
<p>It gave the following percentage changes (month-on-month unless stated)</p>
<p>					    Nov    Oct     Sep   Nov yr/yr</p>
<p> Total				   -0.8   -3.0    -1.2	  0.2</p>
<p> Retail sector			  2.7    2.5    -5.1	  1.9</p>
<p> Durables				-5.3  -13.2     5.2	 -0.8</p>
<p>   of which cars		    -20.9  -25.8    19.2	 -9.3</p>
<p>   household equip		    6.3   -0.8    -5.7	  4.6</p>
<p> Textiles, leather		    2.5    7.3    -9.5	 -0.3</p>
<p> Other				    0.6    0.5    -2.2	  1.0</p>
<p>INSEE originally said consumer spending fell 2.6 percent in October.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
